	<h1>About</h1>

	<!-- TODO(Kareem): replace with your real bio, years of experience, and specific background -->
	<p>
		I manage Google Ads and Meta Ads accounts with one question driving every decision: is this
		spend actually producing revenue, or just activity? Most PPC management stops at clicks,
		conversions, and ROAS as reported by the platform &mdash; numbers that are easy to inflate and
		easy to misread. I start from attribution: what's the platform's reported conversion actually
		worth, and does the account structure reflect how customers really buy.
	</p>

	<h2>How I work</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Account audits that look past surface-level metrics into conversion tracking accuracy, wasted spend, and structural issues.</li>
		<li>Hands-on account management &mdash; not a "set it and forget it" retainer.</li>
		<li>Straight answers about what's working, what isn't, and why &mdash; including when the honest answer is "spend less here."</li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		<a href="/contact/">Want a second opinion on your account?</a>
	</p>
